SkyRL
=====

This project is built on SkyRL (https://github.com/NovaSky-AI/SkyRL), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. SkyRL is an external dependency, used unmodified and import-only; it is not part of this
repository. pyproject.toml installs a checkout of NovaSky-AI/SkyRL at commit
ecdaa9460e281774638a9170d6724456f46c8356, expected next to this repository at ../SkyRL-ecdaa946, through
[tool.uv.sources] (the skyrl and skyrl-gym packages, editable). No SkyRL file is modified.

Files under opsd/skyrl_ext/ that adapt SkyRL source code carry an "Adapted from SkyRL" header that names the
upstream file and what was changed. They are listed, together with the tests that hold them to the upstream
source, in ADAPTED_FROM_SKYRL.md.


Third-party material
====================

This repository builds on, adapts, or interoperates with the following third-party work. Benchmark data and
simulators are not redistributed here; they are fetched at setup time from their official sources.

verl-agent (https://github.com/langfengQ/verl-agent) -- Apache-2.0
    The ALFWorld environment semantics and prompt templates (as used by SDAR) in opsd/envs/alfworld/: the
    prompt templates are reproduced verbatim, the reward and validity semantics are ported.

ALFWorld (https://github.com/alfworld/alfworld) and TextWorld (https://github.com/microsoft/TextWorld) -- MIT
    Installed into a separate simulator virtual environment by scripts/setup/setup_alfworld.sh; the game data
    is downloaded with alfworld-download.

AppWorld (https://github.com/StonyBrookNLP/appworld) -- Apache-2.0
    The simulator is installed into a separate virtual environment by scripts/setup/setup_appworld.sh.
    opsd/appworld/official_react_instructions.txt is the official ReAct prompt (byte-identical to
    experiments/prompts/react_code_agent/instructions.txt). AppWorld data and derivatives may only be
    redistributed in encrypted form: this project's AppWorld-derived artifacts ship only inside an encrypted
    bundle.

tau2-bench (https://github.com/sierra-research/tau2-bench) @ 1d244f5dca42944b67a379b44bfeb9f5748f189d -- MIT
    Cloned at setup time and imported from that checkout (opsd/tau2_bench/source.py); never pip-installed.
    The task-id manifests are in opsd/tau2_bench/data/.

AReaL-tau2-data (https://huggingface.co/datasets/inclusionAI/AReaL-tau2-data) -- Apache-2.0
    The retail RL task pool, downloaded from the Hugging Face Hub at a pinned revision
    (opsd/tau2_bench/areal.py).

Qwen3 chat templates -- Apache-2.0
    opsd/alfworld/qwen3thinking_preserve.jinja2 is derived from the Qwen3-4B-Thinking-2507 chat template.

RLSD (arXiv:2604.03128) -- method citation
    The sign-preserving multiplicative self-distillation arm (opsd/trainer/rlsd.py) implements the published
    method.

SDAR (arXiv:2605.15155) -- method citation
    The gated loss-side distillation term (opsd/algorithms/distill_loss.py, applied in
    opsd/skyrl_ext/policy_worker.py) implements the published method.

SDPO (arXiv:2601.20802) -- method citation
    The ema and trust-region hinted-teacher modes (opsd/trainer/teacher_regularization.py, wired in
    opsd/trainer/main_opsd_alfworld.py) implement the published teacher-regularization constructions.


Model outputs
=============

The privileged-information artifacts (reference trajectories and hints) distributed alongside this code
were generated with third-party models (GLM, Qwen, DeepSeek, Kimi, MiniMax, and OpenAI models used as the
tau2-bench user simulator and judge). Users are responsible for complying with the respective providers'
terms when using those artifacts.
